The best rainbow is the one after a storm. You have to wait for it. The sky is still grey and the rain is stopping. Then the sun comes out and makes a big, bright bow.

I like the double rainbow best. It is very rare. You see the main one, strong and clear. Then, if you look closely, there is a faint second one above it. The colours are in a different order. That feels like a secret.

I also like the rainbow you see in a puddle. You are walking home, feeling cross about wet socks. Then you look down and see the colours in the water. It is a small surprise.

But my favourite is the one you share. You grab your friend's arm and say, "Look!" Everyone stops and points. For a moment, nobody is cross or tired. We all just stand there, smiling at the sky. That is the best rainbow of all. [end of text]


